<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Twenty-seventh Dynasty of Egypt</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as 27th Dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Twenty-seventh Dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> is the name given to the first period of Persian rule over Egypt, beginning with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambyses-ii">Cambyses II</a>'s conquest in 525 BCE. Achaemenid kings ruled Egypt as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaohs</a> through a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrapy">satrap</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a> discuss it as part of the empire's foundational expansion, which brought Egypt into the largest empire the world had yet seen.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/twenty-seventh-dynasty-of-egypt.jpg" alt="Twenty-seventh Dynasty of Egypt" width="320" height="324" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mossmaps · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Western_part_of_the_Achaemenid_Empire.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
